CONVERSION AND EXISTENCE CHECKS
empty_terms_allowed: 28 explicit E/I conversion variants; 26 valid.
all_terms_nonempty: 28 explicit E/I conversion variants; 28 valid.
A_nonempty_only: 28 explicit E/I conversion variants; 28 valid.
A(A,B) => A(B,A): INVALID
E(A,B) => E(B,A): VALID
I(A,B) => I(B,A): VALID
O(A,B) => O(B,A): INVALID
I(A,B) => O(A,B): INVALID in all three regimes.
Under A5's premises, I(C,A) iff A is nonempty: True

FIXED-FIRST-PREMISE AUDIT
Each row checks 128 candidates: 16 second premises x 8 endpoint conclusions.
Matching always permits bijective term renaming and E/I conversion.
Ordered matching keeps premise order; unordered matching also exchanges the premises.
Neither matching adds subalternation or chains derived rules.
Additional candidates are not automatically historical omissions; see PROOF.md.
