FOCUSED COMMON-SUBJECT CASE
A(A,B) & A(A,C) => I(C,B)
  empty_terms_allowed: INVALID
  all_terms_nonempty: VALID
  A_nonempty_only: VALID
A valid existence-dependent common-subject case absent from the nine displayed formulas under either explicit matching convention. Historical 'form' equivalence may be broader; no claim to have reconstructed it.

EXPLICIT NAMED EXAMPLES
A5_empty_A_counterexample: A5 fails with A empty even when B and C are nonempty
  universe=['b']; terms={'A': [], 'B': ['b'], 'C': ['b']}
  premises=A(A,B) & A(B,C); true=True
  conclusion=I(C,A); true=False
I_does_not_imply_O: One shared witness, no witness in A minus B
  universe=['p']; terms={'A': ['p'], 'B': ['p'], 'C': ['p']}
  premises=I(A,B); true=True
  conclusion=O(A,B); true=False
common_subject_empty_A_counterexample: A(A,B) and A(A,C) do not ensure I(C,B) when A is empty
  universe=['b', 'c']; terms={'A': [], 'B': ['b'], 'C': ['c']}
  premises=A(A,B) & A(A,C); true=True
  conclusion=I(C,B); true=False
no_inference_from_A_subset_B_and_C_disjoint_A: C disjoint from B
  universe=['a', 'b', 'c']; terms={'A': ['a'], 'B': ['a', 'b'], 'C': ['c']}
  premises=A(A,B) & E(C,A); true=True
  C-to-B A/E/I/O={'A': False, 'E': True, 'I': False, 'O': True}
no_inference_from_A_subset_B_and_C_disjoint_A: C wholly in B
  universe=['a', 'b', 'c']; terms={'A': ['a'], 'B': ['a', 'b'], 'C': ['b']}
  premises=A(A,B) & E(C,A); true=True
  C-to-B A/E/I/O={'A': True, 'E': False, 'I': True, 'O': False}
no_inference_from_A_subset_B_and_C_disjoint_A: C partially overlaps B
  universe=['a', 'b', 'c']; terms={'A': ['a'], 'B': ['a', 'b'], 'C': ['b', 'c']}
  premises=A(A,B) & E(C,A); true=True
  C-to-B A/E/I/O={'A': False, 'E': False, 'I': True, 'O': True}
pear_tree_equality_counterexample: A=trees, B=pear trees; inclusion and some pears allow equality
  universe=['pear']; terms={'A': ['pear'], 'B': ['pear'], 'C': []}
  premises=A(B,A) & I(A,B); true=True
  conclusion=O(A,B); true=False
pear_tree_strict_inclusion_example: A=trees, B=pear trees; the extra non-pear tree supplies strictness
  universe=['pear', 'oak']; terms={'A': ['pear', 'oak'], 'B': ['pear'], 'C': []}
  premises=A(B,A) & O(A,B); true=True
  conclusion=O(A,B); true=True

